    "innerPrompt": "Basic Descriptive Sentences with Third Person Singular Conjugation\n- Part of Speech Combination: NOUN (singular) + VERB (third person singular present tense) + ADJ\n\n- Focus: The learner should practice forming simple short  sentences with a subject in the singular form (NOUN), a simple action conjugated in the third person singular present tense (VERB), and a descriptor (ADJ).\n\n- Examples:\n    'El gato (NOUN) es (VERB) pequeño (ADJ).' (The cat is small.)\n    'El perro (NOUN) corre (VERB) rápido (ADJ).' (The dog runs fast.)\n    'La sopa (NOUN) huele (VERB) deliciosa (ADJ).' (The soup smells delicious.)\n\nUse the proposed VERB."
